From 9310907bf114afc3dfc1a3068eb7bd421dcbc033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SophiaWJ <jingwangsophia@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:51:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gpui: Composite 32BGRA paint_surface pixel buffers
 premultiplied

`paint_surface` took only 4:2:0 YCbCr video frames: the Metal renderer
asserted the pixel format and drew them opaque, which is what screen
sharing needs. A renderer that draws into an IOSurface-backed BGRA
pixel buffer (a 3D view, a canvas drawn by wgpu or Metal) had no way to
show that texture in place without copying it through memory first.

Accept `kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA` pixel buffers too. Their one plane is
sampled texel for texel through a second surface pipeline whose blend
has source factor one and destination factor one minus source alpha,
because such a buffer holds color premultiplied by alpha: a texel with
color and zero alpha, as a glow beyond an object's edge leaves behind,
still adds its light to what is behind it. YCbCr surfaces are unchanged.

The test renders a BGRA surface headlessly over the opaque black target
and checks a half-covered red texel keeps its premultiplied value, where
a straight-alpha blend halves it, and a zero-alpha green texel keeps its
light, where dividing alpha out loses it.
